{\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow we need to output as JSON with escaped string. We'll produce:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        gain = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"] - call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        normalized_gain = gain / call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"}\n\nMake sure to escape backslashes, quotes, newlines. Use double quotes for JSON string.\n\nLet's double-check: The code uses double quotes inside, so we need to escape them as \\\" . Also newlines as \\n.\n\nI'll write the JSON string carefully."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1932,"completion_tokens":2338,"total_tokens":4270,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2119},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":12},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}